I'd call that a bug in the documentation. It's not actually difficult to
acquire all the available gold and gems, it's merely tedious, so as a
measure of skill, wealth is way down the list.

>> Why go there?
>
> Generally, if you decide to carry more wealth you restrict yourself from
> carrying more useful objects that you need. It's a trade-off; you should
> decide whether to go for some more score points or increase survivability.

There are many such tradeoffs. For example, ascending in as few turns as
possible certainly requires much more careful strategy and restricts your
HP and AC somewhat, since increasing those costs time. It also restricts
your equipment by cutting down stash management time. The turn counter is
easily measurable and the skills required clearly trump those for wealth.

